{"lc": 1, "type": "constructor", "id": ["langchain", "schema", "document", "Document"], "kwargs": {"metadata": {"thread_id": "515452_515451", "turn_ids": ["515452_515451", "515450_515448", "515447_515446", "515445_515444"], "root_turns": ["515452_515451"]}, "page_content": "Customer: text: @SpotifyCares Hi-I have been adding missing songs to my playlists from my Local Files and this has worked great until today. Today, when I drop and drop my local files to my playlist it replaces them with wrong approximate matches. How do I stop this?\nAgent: text: @238736 Hey Andy! Can you try to edit the track name before uploading the file? Let us know how it goes /SJ\n  Customer: text: @SpotifyCares Well, then the name of the song would be wrong.\n  Agent: text: @238736 We understand, but we're just making sure that we cover all bases. You can just edit a single letter of the track name if you don't want to fully change it. Keep us posted /SJ\n    Customer: text: @SpotifyCares Those need to be distinct. How can I just turn off the Spotify algorithm? Spotify doesn\u2019t have the songs so I have to use local files\n    Agent: text: @238736 We're afraid that's currently not possible, but we can see how that\u2019d be useful! We\u2019d recommend suggesting it in our Community where you can get support from other fans: https://t.co/D6JsbrPT3P /PL\n      Customer: text: @SpotifyCares This is really bad news. I had been slowly being weaned off of my iTunes library due to the Local Files but now I will stay with iTunes\n      Agent: text: @238736 We're sorry you feel that way. Not to worry, we'll make sure to give our devs a nudge on this straight away /MT", "type": "Document"}}